tinacloud-completion-bash(1) -- Generate bash completion script
===============================================================

## DESCRIPTION

Generate a bash completion script.

First, ensure "bash-completion" is installed via your package manager.

Try it for the current session:
	source <(tinacloud completion bash)

Persist it by adding this to your ~/.bash_profile:
	eval "$(tinacloud completion bash)"

## SYNOPSIS

`tinacloud completion bash`

## EXAMPLES

	$ echo 'eval "$(tinacloud completion bash)"' >> ~/.bash_profile

